        <para id="para-00034">
          Up until middle adulthood (or age-44 of five-year brackets) unintentional injuries have been the leading cause of death. Previous chapters noted drowning in early childhood and later automobile accidents. In 2020, poisoning (drug overdose) accounts for 62.1% of accidental deaths between the ages of 35 and 64 in the United States with automobile accidents constituting 19.9% (CDC, 2020). 
        </para>
        <para id="para-00035">
          As middle-age, continues the main cause of death shifts to cancers. Cancers form when the body’s normal elimination of old cells is disrupted and damaged cells continue to reproduce. There are numerous risk factors associated with the development of cancers. This can be the result of specific genetics or environmental influences. For example, viruses such as the human papilloma virus (HPV) and Epstein-Barr virus, or chemical exposure to asbestos, frequent and high quantity exposure to radiation can increase risk of cancer, as seen in <link target-id="Figure03_04_CorpusCall"/>. (American Cancer Society, 2023).
        </para> 
          <figure id="Figure03_04_CorpusCall">
            <media alt="Part a and part b both show paintings depicting mixed race families.">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Figure04_03_SleepCycle.png"/>
            </media>
              <caption><emphasis effect="italics">Castas</emphasis> paintings from the mid-1700s document the cultural blending seen in Spanish colonies. Do these images support the assertion that there was a degree of social mobility in the Spanish colonies? Why or why not? </caption>
          </figure>
        <para id="para-00038">Despite changes in the leading cause of deaths in the middle adulthood age demographic, cardiovascular disease (CVD) is a steady and consistent number 2. While CVD is not random it can often be unexpected. There are a number of contributing factors related to cardiovascular health.</para>
        <note class="link-to-learning" id="note-00006">
          <para id="para-00043">
            WW-test notes that this feature tests index terms in a feature. Dynamic Systems provides bar code traceable software and helps companies track the costs associated with production. Not understanding <link url="http://www.a-barcode.com/blog/job-costing-vs-process-costing-whats-the-difference/#.Wcq0S9VSzIU">the difference between job order cost systems and process cost systems</link> is common as customers often ask if their job order cost software is also the process cost software.
          </para>
        </note>
        <para id="para-00044">
          One contributing factor is hypertension or high blood pressure which occurs when the blood pushes against the artery walls at a high force. Another factor is CVD is Cholesterol. Cholesterol is a component of cell membranes made up of proteins and fats. High-density lipoprotein (HDL) is thought of as good cholesterol and cycles through the blood and liver. Low-density lipoprotein (LDL) is thought of as problematic because high amounts will stick to the lining of blood vessels. This causes a hardening of arteries and increases cardiovascular disease and stroke risk. Relatedly, triglycerides, a plaque buildup in the arteries, also increase these risks.
        </para>
    </section>



  <section class="references" id="sect-00013">
    <title>References Option A</title>
    <para id="para-00045">4-Day Week Global. (2023). The results are in: The UK’s four-day week pilot. <emphasis effect="italics">Autonomy</emphasis>. https://static1.squarespace.com/static/60b956cbe7bf6f2efd86b04e/t/63f3df56276b3e6d7870207e/1676926845047/UK-4-Day-Week-Pilot-Results-Report-2023.pdf</para>
