  <section class="summary" id="sect-00014">
    <list id="list-00004">
      <item>Infants come into this world with an individual uniqueness known as temperament.</item>
     <item> Temperament can be shaped and modified by parents and culture, and can predict personality traits that show up later in childhood and adolescence.</item> 
      <item>In the first few years of life, we face psychosocial situations which help us to develop a sense of trust in others and self-confidence and autonomy in ourselves.</item> 
     <item>WW-test notes that this section summary includes <emphasis effect="bold">bold</emphasis>, <emphasis effect="italics">italic</emphasis></item>
    </list> 
  </section>
